 "text": "Hello! How's everything today? Pick a spot in the open where you can set up your tent without blocking anyone else. Most campsites have a layout plan, so check that first. That' usually the most sheltered spot, so it gets busy. If you want be by water, check the edge of the site by the toilets. Pop up the teepee first and check all the pegs and guy ropes are in place. Some branches are just dead branches, others might be roots. Avoid the very center, it's usually the hottest spot. Pick a spot close enough for the evening fire and far enough away from the outhouse. Exactly. And keep your tent door open at night so you don't overheat.",
